<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="ws_1_4" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>Practice Worksheet</title>



<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Find the horizontal and vertical intercepts of the following or state that they don't exist.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=3x-1.5</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Setting <m>y=0</m>, then <m>0=3x-1.5</m> and so <m>1.5=3x</m> implying that <m>x=1 /2</m> is the horizontal intercept. The vertical intercept is when <m>x=0</m>, so <m>y=-1.5</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(x)=1-x^2</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Setting <m>f(x)=0</m>, then <m>0=1-x^2</m> and so <m>x^2=1</m>. Thus <m>x=1</m> and <m>x=-1</m> are the horizontal intercepts. The vertical intercept is when <m>x=0</m>, so <m>y=1</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>g(t)=5.4-0.2t</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Setting <m>g(t)=0</m>, then <m>5.4-0.2t=0</m> and so <m>t=27</m> is the horizontal intercept. When <m>t=0</m>, then <m>y=5.4</m> is the vertical intercept.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=2x^3+16</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Setting <m>y=0</m>, then <m>2x^3+16=0</m> and so <m>2x^3=-16</m>. Thus <m>x^3=-8</m> implying that <m>x=\sqrt[3]{-8} </m> is the horizontal intercept. When <m>x=0</m>, then <m>y=16</m> is the vertical intercept.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>h(m)=2\sqrt{m}-3</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Setting <m>h(m)=0</m>, then <m>2\sqrt{m} -3=0</m> so <m>2\sqrt{m} =3</m>. Thus <m>\sqrt{m}  = 3 /2</m> implying that <m>m = (3 /2)^2 = 9 /4</m>. The vertical intercept is <m>y=-3</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\dfrac{1}{x}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Note that <m>y</m> can never be <m>0</m>, so there are no horizontal intercepts. And, <m>x</m> cannot be <m>0</m> so there are no vertical intercepts either.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\dfrac{1}{x-1}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Note that <m>y</m> can never be <m>0</m>, so there are no horizontal intercepts. But there is a vertical intercept when <m>x=0</m>, and this is <m>y=-1</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>
 



<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
For each of the following, find the horizontal and vertical intercepts or state that there is not enough information to determine them.
</p>
</introduction>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<tabular left="minor" right="minor" top="minor" bottom="minor" halign="center">
<row bottom="minor">
<cell><m>x</m></cell>
<cell><m>-2</m></cell>
<cell><m>-1</m></cell>
<cell><m>0</m></cell>
<cell><m>1</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell><m>y</m></cell>
<cell><m>3</m></cell>
<cell><m>0</m></cell>
<cell><m>2</m></cell>
<cell><m>2.5</m></cell>
<cell><m>0</m></cell>
<cell><m>4</m></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
Vertical intercept is <m>y=2</m>, horizontal intercepts are <m>x=-1</m> and <m>x=2</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<tabular left="minor" right="minor" top="minor" bottom="minor" halign="center">
